hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"915","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a slave obeys his Lord and his master, he will have two rewards."
"916","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The person who hears a word of wisdom and understanding, but takes what he hears in a bad manner—his example is like that of a man who comes to a shepherd and says: O shepherd! Give me a goat from your goats for meat. The shepherd says: Go and catch the best goat. So he (goes and) grabs the ear of the herd's dog."
"917","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Grant sustenance to the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) according to their need."
"918","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I was walking in the date gardens of Madinah in the company of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when he said: ""Abu Hurairah! Those who possess much wealth will be ruined. Indeed, those who possess much wealth will be the lowest, except for the one who spends like this, like this, and like this,"" meaning in front of him, behind him, to his right, and to his left. Then he narrated to the end as in the previous hadith (No. 266, 265)."
"919","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah says: Grandeur is My cloak and honor is My «إزار» , so whoever tries to snatch either of them from Me, I will throw him into Hell."
"920","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: We said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the matter with us that when we are with you, it is as if our hearts are attached to the Hereafter, but when we leave you and meet our families, this state leaves us?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If your state after leaving me remained as it is when you are with me, then the angels would shake hands with you with their hands, visit you in your homes, and if you did not commit sins, Allah would bring people who would commit sins and then be forgiven."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Tell me, from what was the creation made?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""From water."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Tell me about Paradise and its construction."" Then the narrator mentioned the narration similar to that of Isa and continued to the end, and said: "" «مسک» (musk) «أذخر» is its mortar and its pebbles are pearls, jewels, and rubies."" And he said: ""The prayer of a just king is not rejected."
"921","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The worst people of my Ummah are those who were brought up in blessings and whose bodies grew upon them."
"922","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever seeks the world in a lawful manner, wanting to avoid asking from others, to fulfill the needs of his family, and to show kindness to his neighbor, then he will come on the Day of Resurrection with his face like the full moon of the fourteenth night. And whoever seeks the world in a lawful manner for boasting, rivalry, and showing off, then he will meet Allah in such a state that He will be angry with him."
"923","With this (previous) chain, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah loves the wise, prudent, and those who avoid asking (unnecessarily), and He dislikes the foul-mouthed, ill-spoken, and those who persistently ask (demandingly)."
"924","And with this, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, he said: ""To the remembrance of Allah, so stop (and pay attention)."
"925","With this (previous) chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said to them: ""Do you know what «نميمة» is?"" They replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is conveying people's words to others in order to create discord among them."" And he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If a man had two valleys full of wealth, he would seek a third valley. Nothing will fill the belly of man except the dust (of the grave), and Allah forgives whom He wills."
"926","With this (previous) chain of narration, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Satan moves within the human body, so when Allah saves him from one door, he comes from another door until he destroys some part of him."
"927","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: It is astonishing that people abandon saying «لا إله إلا الله» and «الله أكبر» ; as for me, I only desire that the takbir be performed well. Satan attacks a person from the direction of sin, so when he is protected from that, then he attacks him from the direction of good deeds so that he may abandon the Sunnah and commit innovation."
"928","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and I saw its inhabitants, and most of them were the poor."
"929","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! Offering one prayer in the mosque of Madinah (the Prophet's Mosque) is better than offering one thousand prayers in other mosques, except for the Ka'bah (the Sacred Mosque in Makkah)."
"930","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""If you were to know what I know, then you would laugh little and weep much, but keep close, remain upright, and accept glad tidings."
"931","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Shall I not tell you about your best people?"" They said: ""Why not."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(Your best people) are those who, when you see them, remind you of Allah. Shall I not tell you about your worst people?"" They said: ""Why not, O Messenger of Allah!"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tale-bearers, those who cause discord between friends, and those who seek corruption and mischief."
"932","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever dislikes to meet Allah, Allah dislikes to meet him. And before meeting Allah, there is death."
"933","Masruq narrated: I went to Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and she was crying. I said to her: O Mother of the Believers! Why are you crying? She replied: I become full from food and I wish to cry, so I begin to cry, and this is because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) never ate his fill of wheat bread twice in one day until he passed away."
"934","Aisha bint Talha narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""The reward for good conduct and maintaining family ties is received the quickest among good deeds, and the punishment for oppression and severing family ties is received the quickest among all evils."
"935","The son of Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from his paternal aunt (Fatimah bint Yaman, may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fell ill, so I, along with some Muhajir women, went to attend to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had hung a water skin, and it was dripping drop by drop onto his chest. I said: O Messenger of Allah! This has caused you pain, pray to Allah to remove this hardship from you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The prophets (peace be upon them all) are tested the most severely, then those nearest to them, and then those who come after them.”"
"936","Lady Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I, along with some women, went to visit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to inquire about his health. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had a water-skin hanging. Then the narrator mentioned the hadith similar to the previous one."
"937","Lady Fatimah (bint Yaman, may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I came into the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) along with some women, and saw that he had hung a water-skin and, due to the pain he was experiencing, its water was being dripped drop by drop onto him. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah that He removes your pain. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The most severe trials come upon all the Prophets (peace be upon them), then those after them, then those after them, and then those after them.”"
"938","Ubaid Sanuta narrated: I went to Umm Muhammad (Khawla bint Qais, may Allah be pleased with her), who was the wife of Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib, may Allah be pleased with him. After him, a man named Hanzala married her. She (Khawla) said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came one day to the daughter of Hamza, and she mentioned the emirates to him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The world is lush and green, so whoever takes from it with its due right, Allah will bless it for that person. Sometimes, for the one who indulges in Allah’s wealth according to his own desires, there will be the fire of Hell on the Day of Resurrection."
"939","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say this often, so I do not know whether it was something he considered preferable or if it is from the Book of Allah: ""If a person has two valleys full of wealth, he will wish for a third like them; nothing will fill his soul except (the grave's) dust. Whoever repents, Allah accepts his repentance."
